@host = http://localhost:5099

# Identity is supplied by header. The role is read from the database record, never from the request,
# so changing this header changes who you are, not what you are allowed to do.
@requester = user-01
@technician = tech-nikau
@otherTechnician = tech-raj
@teamLead = lead-maia

### Liveness
GET {{host}}/api/health

### Accounts available in the role switcher
GET {{host}}/api/users

### Priority bands and their configured targets
GET {{host}}/api/reference/priorities

### Open queue, as the service manager
GET {{host}}/api/tickets?openOnly=true
X-User-Id: {{teamLead}}

### Open queue, as a technician — restricted tickets they do not hold are absent
GET {{host}}/api/tickets?openOnly=true
X-User-Id: {{technician}}

### A requester sees only their own tickets
GET {{host}}/api/tickets
X-User-Id: {{requester}}

### Unassigned critical work
GET {{host}}/api/tickets?priority=Critical&unassignedOnly=true&openOnly=true
X-User-Id: {{teamLead}}

### Raise a ticket
POST {{host}}/api/tickets
X-User-Id: {{requester}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Concession POS terminal offline at gate 4",
  "description": "The tenant cannot take card payments and the departure peak starts in an hour.",
  "category": "Point of Sale",
  "priority": "Critical"
}

### One ticket with its audit trail
GET {{host}}/api/tickets/1
X-User-Id: {{teamLead}}

### Triage
POST {{host}}/api/tickets/1/transition
X-User-Id: {{technician}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "status": "Triaged" }

### Self-assign
POST {{host}}/api/tickets/1/assign
X-User-Id: {{technician}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "technicianId": "tech-nikau" }

### Refused: a technician cannot assign work to a colleague (403)
POST {{host}}/api/tickets/1/assign
X-User-Id: {{technician}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "technicianId": "tech-raj" }

### Start work — this stops the response clock
POST {{host}}/api/tickets/1/transition
X-User-Id: {{technician}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "status": "InProgress" }

### Park the ticket — this suspends the resolution clock
POST {{host}}/api/tickets/1/transition
X-User-Id: {{technician}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "status": "OnHold", "note": "Awaiting the tenant to reopen the till." }

### Refused: resolving without notes (400)
POST {{host}}/api/tickets/1/transition
X-User-Id: {{technician}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "status": "Resolved" }

### Resolve with notes
POST {{host}}/api/tickets/1/transition
X-User-Id: {{technician}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "status": "Resolved", "note": "Replaced the card reader and confirmed a test transaction." }

### Refused: a technician cannot close (403)
POST {{host}}/api/tickets/1/transition
X-User-Id: {{technician}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "status": "Closed" }

### The requester closes
POST {{host}}/api/tickets/1/transition
X-User-Id: {{requester}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "status": "Closed" }

### Refused: a technician cannot reprioritise (403)
POST {{host}}/api/tickets/2/priority
X-User-Id: {{technician}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "priority": "Critical", "justification": "Looks urgent to me" }

### The service manager reprioritises, with a reason for the audit trail
POST {{host}}/api/tickets/2/priority
X-User-Id: {{teamLead}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "priority": "Critical", "justification": "Tenant trading impact confirmed with the duty manager." }

### Comment — a comment from support staff records first response
POST {{host}}/api/tickets/2/comments
X-User-Id: {{technician}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "comment": "Attending site now; will update within the hour." }

### Refused: reporting is closed to technicians (403)
GET {{host}}/api/reports/summary
X-User-Id: {{technician}}

### Management report, last 30 days
GET {{host}}/api/reports/summary
X-User-Id: {{teamLead}}
